    "summary": "This sword features a long, straight, single-edged steel blade that widens near the tip. The hilt is carved from dark hardwood and takes the shape of a stylized zoomorphic figure, possibly a bird, <em>buwaya</em> (crocodile), or <em>naga</em>. The materials, carving style, and blade form correspond to <em>kampilan</em>-type swords made among the Maranao and Maguindanao people of northern and central Mindanao.",
